  displayName: "Tango"
  style: 1
  origin: "Buenos Aires (Argentina) and Montevideo (Uruguay)"
  history: "Tango was born in the port neighborhoods of the Rio de la Plata in the late 1800s, mixing European, African and local influences. It became a craze in Paris around 1912 to 1913, and English teachers later reshaped it into the sharp, staccato ballroom Tango. Unlike the other Standard dances it has no rise and fall."
  timeSignature: "2/4"
  tempoMinBarsPerMinute: 31
  tempoMaxBarsPerMinute: 33
  difficulty: 3
  characteristics:
  - "Sharp and dramatic"
  - "Staccato (stop-and-go) movement"
  - "No rise and fall"
  - "Flat, cat-like walks"
  skills:
  - "Quick head and leg actions"
  - "A compact, strong hold"
  - "Precise rhythm and timing"
  - "Grounded posture with flexed knees"
